artifact.existingSchema:
CREATE TABLE companies (
  id BIGSERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
  code VARCHAR(16) NOT NULL,
  name VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  tax_code VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL,
  address VARCHAR(512) NOT NULL,
  logo_url VARCHAR(512),
  created_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW(),
  updated_at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT NOW()
);
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ux_companies_code ON companies(code);
CREATE UNIQUE INDEX ux_companies_tax_code ON companies(tax_code);
ALTER TABLE companies ADD CONSTRAINT ck_tax_code_digits CHECK (tax_code ~ '^[0-9]{10}$');

constraints.databaseMigrations:
- Use Flyway versioned migrations: V{number}__{description}.sql
- Next available version: V8 or V9 (check existing migrations)
- Migration file: V8__add_company_contact_fields.sql
- ALTER TABLE companies ADD COLUMN contact_email VARCHAR(255);
- ALTER TABLE companies ADD COLUMN contact_phone VARCHAR(20);
- ALTER TABLE companies ADD COLUMN legal_representative VARCHAR(255);
- ALTER TABLE companies ADD COLUMN fiscal_year_start INTEGER DEFAULT 1;
- Add CHECK constraint: fiscal_year_start >= 1 AND fiscal_year_start <= 12
- Never modify existing migrations (V1__companies.sql is immutable)

interface.supabaseIntegration:
- Bucket: "company-logos" (create if not exists)
- Access: public read, authenticated write
- File path: {companyId}/logo-{timestamp}.{ext}
- Scaled paths: {companyId}/logo-{timestamp}-header.{ext}, -footer.{ext}
- Use image processing library (e.g., Thumbnailator) for scaling

interface.validationLogic:
Optional<Company> existing = repository.findByTaxCode(taxCode);
if (existing.isPresent() && !existing.get().getId().equals(currentCompanyId)) {
  throw new ResponseStatusException(HttpStatus.CONFLICT, 
    "Tax code already exists for company: " + existing.get().getName());
}
